+# Olympus layer: the look, Day timeline, Focus mode
+
+Plain text for the Help sheet and README (merge by hand). The owner asked for "way higher quality, 3D UI effects",
+"organized like a maid swept" and "futuristic".
+
+## The look
+- Cards have depth: soft layered shadows, a faint accent sheen, rounded corners. In dark mode they are glass (the aurora
+  shows through). Light mode keeps every colour it had.
+- A soft aurora sits behind the page and glides to a new place when you switch views; cards rise in then, and tilt a
+  little under the mouse. Buttons press in when tapped. A ticked task pops, with a short buzz on phones that can.
+- Today, tidied: the date on one line, the header buttons in one even row on a phone, quiet section labels with a hairline,
+  the status line with a dot (green when nothing is urgent, red when something needs you) and a tighter rhythm on phones.
+- **Off switch:** palette "Olympus effects off" (this device). The Olympus 3D quality setting is followed too: Off = plain
+  look, Low = no motion. When the phone asks for reduced motion, nothing moves.
+- **Olympus themes:** the theme picked in Olympus (Jarvis) recolours the accents (aurora, timeline, Focus ring). No theme =
+  the default indigo and cyan.
+
+## Day timeline (Today, joined to the status line)
+- Today's events on one track from 7am to 10pm (wider if your day is), overlaps in a second or third lane, with a glowing
+  NOW beam; what is on now glows. It sits inside the status line ("3 things need you · next: Dentist 2pm"), one unit, so the
+  busy Today is no longer than before. Tap a block to open the event. **Focus** (first in the header's button row) opens
+  Focus mode.
+- A clear day (no events, no tasks) shows "Your day is wide open" with **Add a task** and **Focus**.
+
+## Focus mode (`#focus-mode`)
+- Full screen, a glowing ring counting down. Pick one of today's tasks and a length (15, 25, 45 or 60 minutes), then
+  **Start focus**. It is the same focus timer as the clock button on a task: minutes are logged on the task the same way.
+- While it runs: **Finish and log** (stop now, log the minutes so far), **Cancel** (no log), **Minimise** (the timer keeps
+  running in the bar at the bottom; tap the time there to come back).
+- At the end: **5 min break** (a green ring), **Another round** or **Close**. It shows the minutes focused today.
+- Also in the palette ("Focus mode") and All tools.
+
+## Notes for the lead (not for the Help sheet)
+- Code: `planner/ext-olympus.js`, loaded by one `<script src="ext-olympus.js">` in `<head>` after ext-flow.js. It waits for
+  `planner:ready` (`window.PlannerAPI`). Nothing else in `index.html` changed.
+- Data: none synced. Focus mode starts the timer through the app's own Focus timer sheet (`openFocus` + its form) and stops it
+  through the timer bar's own buttons, so `S.focus`, logging and Undo are the app's. The break lives in memory only. Device
+  keys: `planner.olympus.fx` (`off` = plain look). Read only: `olympus.theme` (Olympus theme), `jfx` (Olympus 3D quality).
+- Theme map: `olympus.theme` is a theme id (Jarvis's Look sheet). Its tokens come from Olympus's `themes.js`
+  (`window.OLYMPUS_THEMES.tokens(id, 'page')`), taken from the Jarvis frame around the Planner (same origin) or loaded once
+  from `../olympus/themes.js`. `accent` -> `--ox-a`, `accent2` -> `--ox-b`, `glow` -> `--ox-glow` (colours only). No key, the
+  default `olympus` theme, an unknown id or no themes.js on the site = the Planner's own accents. A JSON object of tokens is
+  accepted too (top level, `.tokens` or `.vars`).
+- The timeline is drawn after each Today render (a MutationObserver on `#main`, before paint) and redrawn every 30 seconds.
+  Height: the busy phone day of todayorg.test.js is 4563 px with it (4560 without; the limit is 4571), so it has no header
+  of its own and phones use a 12 px card gap. Only compositor-cheap animations run forever (transform / opacity, no blur
+  filters, no endless full-screen motion; the aurora moves once per view change): the Planner's own timing-sensitive
+  tests stay green.
+- Light-mode colours of the theme test's key elements are unchanged (depth uses shadows and background images only).
+- Pure helpers on `window.__ox`: `level`, `themeVars`, `line`, `state`, `applyLook`.
+- Tests: `planner/tests/olympus.test.js` (PORT env, default 8789; 47 checks).
